matrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186054552 1074 "We subtract the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-0 & -1-(-1) \\\\ -1-2 & 0-(-1) \\\\ 3-(-1) & 2-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186054553 1071 "Calculate ${A}+ {B}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186054553 1071 "Calculate ${A}+ {B},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186054553 1074 "We add the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA + B &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 + (-2) & 3 + (-3) & 1 + 1 & 0 + 1 \\\\ 2 + 1 & 4 + (-2) & -1 + 3 & 2 + 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186054553 1074 "We add the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+(-2) & 3+(-3) & 1+1 & 0+1 \\\\ 2+1 & 4+(-2) & -1+3 & 2+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059499 1071 "Express $\\sin\\left(x - 30^{\\circ} \\right )$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x.$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059499 1071 "Express $\\sin\\left(x - 30^{\\circ} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059499 1074 "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u\\cos v - \\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and\n\n$$\nv=30^{\\circ}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (x - 30^{∘}) &= \\sin x\\cos 30^{∘} - \\cos x\\sin 30^{∘} \\\\\n&= \\sin x \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) - \\cos x \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2} - \\frac{\\cos x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x - \\cos x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059499 1074 "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u\\cos v - \\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=30^{\\circ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059500 1071 "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.*" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059500 1071 "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.$*" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059500 1074 "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3} - \\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3})\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}) - \\cos (\\frac{π}{3})\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059500 1074 "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ and $y = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059502 1071 "Express $\\cos\\left( x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x.$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059502 1071 "Express $\\cos\\left(x - \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059502 1074 "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u - v) = \\cos u \\cos v + \\sin u \\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u = x$ and\n\n$$\nv = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (x - \\frac{π}{2}) &= \\cos x\\cos (\\frac{π}{2}) + \\sin x\\sin (\\frac{π}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\cos x \\cdot 0 + \\sin x \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= \\sin x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059502 1074 "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u - v) = \\cos u \\cos v + \\sin u \\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u = x$ and $v = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059503 1071 "Find the exact value of $\\cos \\left( -\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} \\right).$\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.$*" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059503 1071 "Find the exact value of $\\cos \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} \\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.*" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059503 1074 "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x - y) = \\cos{x}\\cos{y} + \\sin{x}\\sin{y}\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (-\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\cos (\\frac{π}{6} - \\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{π}{6})\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}) + \\sin (\\frac{π}{6})\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059503 1074 "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x - y) = \\cos{x}\\cos{y} + \\sin{x}\\sin{y}\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ and $y = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059505 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin 15^{∘}\\cos 15^{∘} &= \\sin (2 \\cdot 15^{∘}) = \\sin 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059505 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059506 1071 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}$." 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059506 1071 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}.$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059506 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})]\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059506 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059507 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}$." 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059507 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}.$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059507 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{\\sin 50^{∘}} &= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sec 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059507 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡{25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059508 1071 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}$." 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186059508 1071 "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}.$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186059508 1074 "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{8}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 2\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}} = 3 \\left(\\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{