{3}{5}.$\n\nUsing the fact that\n\n$$\n\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta},\n$$\n\nwe finally get\n\n$$\n\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)} = \\dfrac {3}{4}.\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186110466 1071 "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\csc \\theta + \\cot \\theta} + \\cot \\theta$." 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186110466 1071 "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\csc \\theta + \\cot \\theta} + \\cot \\theta.$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186110466 1074 "First, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n1= \\csc^2{\\theta} -\\cot^2{\\theta}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{\\csc θ + \\cot θ} + \\cot θ &= \\frac{\\csc^{2} θ - \\cot^{2} θ}{\\csc θ + \\cot θ} + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= ((\\csc θ - \\cot θ)(\\csc θ + \\cot θ))/(\\csc θ + \\cot θ) + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= ((\\csc θ - \\cot θ)(\\csc θ + \\cot θ))/(\\csc θ + \\cot θ) + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= (\\csc θ - \\cot θ) + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= \\csc θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186110466 1074 "First, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n1= \\csc^2{\\theta} -\\cot^2{\\theta}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }+\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )\\,\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operator