3\\sqrt{3}) \\cdot (-2(-1)^{1 + 1}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (-9) \\cdot ((-2) \\cdot (-5 + 4)) \\\\\n&= (-9) \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&=-18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119599 1071 "Find $\\mid A^{-1} \\mid$, if $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119599 1071 "Find $|A^{-1}|,$ if  ![](images/8a/8a5169c6a418a8ddaa9b3478e535039b253724ae622692ea728b2a94dc112e4a.png)" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186119599 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}A^{-1} & = \\dfrac{1}{\\mid A\\end{vmatrix}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $\\mid A \\mid$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}A & &= & 2 & 14\\end{vmatrix}- 1 \\\\\n&= 7\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}0 \\mid \\\\\n&=-3(-1)^{3 + 2}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-12 + 7) \\\\\n&=-15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) = \\dfrac{1}{\\mid A \\mid} = -\\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119599 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|A^{-1}| = \\dfrac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-12+7) \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) =  \\dfrac{1}{|A|} = -\\dfrac{1}{15}.\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186119600 1071 "Given that\n$\\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}$\nfind\n$\\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119600 1071 "Given that \n!