$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186119606 1071 "Let $\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. Find $z$.\n${x - y + 3z =-1; 4x - 2z = 1; 3x + y - z =-2$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119606 1071 "Let $\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. Find $z.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4x-2z=1 \\\\ 3x+y-z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186119606 1074 "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{1x- 1y + 3z =-1; 4x + 0y- 2z = 1; 3x + 1y- 1z =-2\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} &= 1 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}- (-1) \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+ 3 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= (0 - (-2)) + (-4 + 6) + 3(4 - 0) \\\\\n&= 2 + 2 + 12 \\\\\n&= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find $D_z$, we take the coefficients matrix, replace the *third* column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{z} =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} &= 1 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}- (-1) \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}+ (-1) \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= (0 - 1) + (-8 - 3) - (4 - 0) \\\\\n&=-1 - 11 - 4 \\\\\n&=-16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= \\frac{D_{z}}{D} = \\frac{-16}{16} =-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119606 1074 "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1x-1y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4x+0y-2z=1 \\\\ 3x+1y-1z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(-4+6)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =2+2+12 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find $D_z,$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the *third* column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-1)+(-8-3)-(4-0) \\\\  & =-1-11-4 \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{-16}{16}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 true] [17592186119607 1071 "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below.\n${5x - 2y = 4; x + ky = 8$\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k$?\n\n1. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$\n2. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$\n3. $\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{vmatrix}$" 13194139533387 17592186045585 false] [17592186119607 1071 "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=4 \\\\ x+